# Field notes

Four illustrative observations refer to three species: [[barn-owl]],
[[european-robin]], [[barn-owl]] again, and [[common-raven]].

A `List<String>` retains every occurrence and its position. Viewing it as
`Seq<String>` retains the positional contract. Viewing it as
`Collection<String>` lets a query ask about membership and multiplicity.

```hql#eval
sightings : List<String> = [
    "barn-owl",
    "european-robin",
    "barn-owl",
    "common-raven",
]
occurrences : Collection<String> = sightings
species : Set<String> = Set(sightings)

{
    observations: size(occurrences),
    barn_owls: count(occurrences, "barn-owl"),
    species: size(species),
    saw_robin: contains(species, "european-robin"),
}
```

There are four occurrences and three distinct species. The list contains two
owl observations; the set contains one owl name. See [[collection-views]] for
keyed counts.
